# Canonical identity mapping for git log + GitHub contributor graph.
#
# Format (per `git help shortlog` / https://git-scm.com/docs/gitmailmap):
#   <canonical-name> <canonical-email>                 <old-email>
#   Proper Name <commit@email>                         <old-email>
#
# When git tools (git shortlog, git log --use-mailmap, GitHub's
# contributor graph) see a commit by an old email or name, they
# substitute the canonical version on the LEFT.
#
# This file does NOT rewrite history -- past commits keep their
# original author metadata in the object database. The mapping is
# applied at READ time only. To include the mapping in your local
# git log, run `git log --use-mailmap` (or set
# `git config --global log.mailmap true` to make it the default).
#
# References:
#   https://git-scm.com/docs/gitmailmap
#   https://docs.github.com/en/account-and-profile/setting-up-and-managing-your-personal-account-on-github/managing-email-preferences/setting-your-commit-email-address

# Ahmed Attia: VT email (older; used for commits 2026-05-13 and earlier
# of this repo) -> ANL email (current canonical).
